Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:00:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/22] run: --yes refuses a dirty git workspace, --allow-dirty
 opts in

--yes hands every mutating call to the model unchecked, so the tree it
lands on is the only safety net: a checkpoint restores what an edit
touched, nothing restores what a bash command removed before any
checkpoint saw it. Uncommitted work is work with no net, and the
combination used to run silently (HARDENING 5.5, still open there).
The guard fires before anything persists or spawns: a git workspace
with entries in status refuses with the count and the escape named;
--allow-dirty says the operator knew; non-git workspaces have no
baseline to protect and pass.

Verified against the real binary: dirty repo + --yes exits 2 with the
refusal, + --allow-dirty runs.
